1
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:22,000
The Horse Whisperer is a adventure, drama, romance
film directed by Robert Redford.

2
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:38,000
The mother of a severely traumatized daughter enlists the aid of a unique
horse trainer to help the girl's equally injured horse.

3
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Tom Booker, played by Robert Redford.

4
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:10,000
Annie MacLean, played by Kristin Scott Thomas.

5
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
Robert MacLean, played by Sam Neill.

6
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
Grace MacLean, played by Scarlett Johansson.

7
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:58,000
Diane Booker, played by Dianne Wiest.

8
01:30:08,000 --> 01:30:14,000
Frank Booker, played by Chris Cooper.

9
01:41:24,000 --> 01:41:30,000
The Horse Whisperer is a 1998 American neo-western drama film directed by and starring
Robert Redford, based on the 1995 novel The Horse Whisperer by Nicholas Evans.

10
01:52:40,000 --> 01:52:46,000
Redford plays the title role, a talented trainer with a remarkable gift for understanding horses, who is hired to help an
injured teenager (played by Scarlett Johansson) and her horse back to health following a tragic accident.

11
02:03:56,000 --> 02:04:02,000
The film was produced by Touchstone Pictures and released on May
15, 1998 by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution.

12
02:15:12,000 --> 02:15:18,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics and
grossed nearly $187 million worldwide.

13
02:26:28,000 --> 02:26:34,000
The film explores themes of new york city, love triangle, attachment
to nature, parent child relationship, marriage crisis.

14
02:37:44,000 --> 02:37:50,000
The tone is emotional.
